<title>USA: Eagle Bancshares Q4 shr $0.35 before charge.</title>
<headline>Eagle Bancshares Q4 shr $0.35 before charge.</headline>
<dateline>TUCKER, Ga. 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Q4 ended March 31	  1997			1996</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.35		    $0.30</p>
<p> Oper net		   1,900		    1,500</p>
<p> Avg shrs			NA			 NA</p>
<p>		 Year</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.66		    $1.40</p>
<p> Net			  3,700		    6,200</p>
<p> Avg shrs			NA			 NA</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: The company said Q4 results do not include merger and restructuring charges associated with the acquisition of Southern Crescent Financial in March. The company did not include details of the effect the charge had on Q4 earnings in its statement. A company spokeswoman was not available.</p>
<p>Year-end results included charges for the merger and for the Savings Association Insurance Fund assessment. Without those charges, year-end net income would have risen 8.1 percent to $6.7 million or $1.21 per share.</p>
<p>Eagle Bancshares had assets totaling $823 million at year end. Year end return on assets was 0.88 percent.</p>
</text>
